  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In a cyclic process, internal energy change $=0$\nAccording to $1^{\\text {st }}$ law of thermodynamics\n$\\Delta U=\\Delta q+\\Delta W$\nAs, $\\Delta U=0, \\quad \\Delta q=-\\Delta W$\nFrom the graph, work done $=\\Delta W=$ Area under curve Here, area of circle $=\\pi r^2$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\pi\\left(\\frac{25-5}{2}\\right)^2=\\pi \\times 10^2 \\\\\n\\therefore \\quad \\Delta q & =100 \\pi \\mathrm{~J}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
